  "body": "## What changed\n\nPart of #372 (decision: the machine's axis really moves the other way; the CAM side stays right-handed per ISO 841).\n\n- **Machine file:** a linear part of a file-form `.mch` takes `\"direction\": 1 | -1`. Absent or null means `1`. Anything else (`0`, `2`, `0.5`, `\"-1\"`, a vector, a bool) refuses at load and names the axis: `machine file: axis X direction must be +1 or -1, not 2`. A numeric `-1` on a rotary part refuses too (a reversed rotary is not supported).\n- **Model:** `AxisLimits::direction: machine::AxisDirection { Standard, Inverted }` (new `crates/post/src/machine/direction.rs`), plus `Machine::inverted_axes()`, `Machine::inverted_post_refusal()` and `AxisLimits::program_travel()`, ready for #374 to read. The project file stores it as `1`/`-1`; a bad value refuses the load. A standard axis writes no key, so every shipped machine, every saved project and the post mirror are byte-identical.\n- **Travel check:** a stated stroke is the machine's own, in the coordinates its controller reads. An inverted axis is judged as `-v` against `[lo, hi]`, and the breach line says `(inverted axis)`. The derived table box maps the stroke to `[-hi, -lo]` in the program frame.\n- **Posting is refused until #374:** the verification gate adds `machine <model> has an inverted X axis; posting for inverted axes is not supported yet (#374)`. That one gate blocks the single post, per-op posts and the script API's gate. The CLI `post --machine` refuses the same way, and now also refuses a file that `parse_mch` refuses. Standard-sign code is never posted for an inverted machine.\n- **Machine page:** the machine editor gets a per-axis choice: \"X+ moves: right / left\", Y \"away / toward you\", Z \"up / down\", other letters \"standard / reversed\". An inverted axis shows a note that posting is refused until #374. The editor edits a draft that is applied through the existing undoable `EditMachineApply` -> `LoadMachine` command, so no new command was needed.\n- Docs: grammar row in `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`; decisions in `docs/decisions/373-axis-direction.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/axis_direction.rs` (11 tests):\n  - `direction_reads_plus_one_minus_one_and_absent`, `any_other_direction_refuses_by_name`, `a_reversed_rotary_refuses_and_other_rotary_shapes_are_not_read`\n  - `every_shipped_machine_stays_standard` (every `posting::MACHINES` entry: no inverted axis, no serialized key, mirror unchanged)\n  - `direction_round_trips_through_serde_and_refuses_garbage`, `an_inverted_machine_survives_a_project_save_and_load`, `loading_an_inverted_machine_undoes`\n  - `travel_is_judged_in_the_machines_own_coordinates`, `the_table_box_maps_an_inverted_stroke`\n  - `an_inverted_machine_refuses_posting_by_name`, `the_refusal_names_every_inverted_axis`\n- `crates/post/tests/axis_direction_cli.rs`: `the_cli_refuses_an_inverted_machine_by_name`\n\n## Gate (quick, debug, this worktree)\n\n- Merged origin/main (#354 one-WCS) cleanly; app suites green after the merge: axis_direction 11, machine 32, tormach_machines 5, posting 17, conformance 6, golden_cl 23, fanuc_post 8, project_roundtrip 69, fixtures 14, setup_sheet 7. The goldens are unchanged.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post` (all suites) green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib` run from `crates/ui`: 297 passed, 2 ignored (after merging origin/main; on the pre-merge base, `egui_shell_snapshot_light` and `tool_editor_snapshot` failed the same way without this change - #354 regenerated those snapshots)\n\nNot tested: the editor's combo by hand (the GUI was not launched), and posting itself for an inverted machine, which is #374.\n\nChangelog: The machine file states a per-axis direction (`\"direction\": -1` on a linear part, shown on the machine editor as \"X+ moves: right / left\"). Travel limits are judged through an inverted axis. Posting for a machine with an inverted axis is refused by name until #374.\n\nFixes #373\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
